==History==
2018
*The Ram Rider was once available in the [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Ram Rider Draft Challenge]] which started on 21/12/2018. In this [[Tournament|challenge]], gameplay was similar to a regular Draft Challenge, except that one of the players was able to choose who would use the Ram Rider. If the player achieved at least 10 wins, they obtained the Ram Rider early.
*The Ram Rider [[Cards|card]] was generally released on 24/12/2018.
2019
*On 28/1/2019, the [[Version History#January%202019%20Update%20(28/1/2019)|January 2019 Update]], changed the Ram Rider's card description. It used to read “''Her bola snares enemy troops while Ram heads for the nearest building! Rams and Hogs don't mingle at parties…''”
*On 1/4/2019, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (1/4/2019)|Balance Update]], decreased the Ram Rider's snare movement speed reduction to 85% (from 100%).
*On 17/5/2019, the Ram Rider's card image was changed. The new image replaces the old image upon a new install; keeping the app installed prior to the update retains the old card image, even if the app is updated.
*On 26/11/2019, the [[Version History#End%20of%20November%202019%20Update%20(26/11/2019)|End of November 2019 Update]], removed the Ram Rider from [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Mega Deck]] [[Touchdown]]. It also added a card render to the Ram Rider's card info screen.
2021
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022 
*On 3/2/2022, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(3/2/2022)|Balance Update]], made it so that the Ram Rider's snare ability would no longer affect the [[:Category:Troop Cards|troop]] spawning of the [[Witch]] and [[Night Witch]].
*On 4/4/2022, the [[Version History#April%202022%20Update%20(4/4/2022)|April 2022 Update]], decreased the Ram Rider's snare movement speed reduction to 70% (from 85%).
*On 2/8/2022, a [[Version History#Balance%20Changes%20(2/8/2022)|Balance Update]], decreased the distance required for charging to 3 tiles (from 3.5 tiles).
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Ram Rider from Hog Mountain to Electro Valley.
2023 
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2024
*On 17/6/2024, the [[Version History#Goblin World Update (17/6/2024)|Goblin World Update]], decreased the distance required for charging to 1.5 tiles (from 3 tiles).
*On 2/7/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (2/7/2024)|Balance Update]], increased the distance required for charging to 2 tiles (from 1.5 tiles).
*On 14/11/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (14/11/2024)|Balance Update]], decreased the Ram Rider's damage and charge damage by 6%.
2025
*On 8/1/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (8/1/2025)|Balance Update]], decreased the Ram Rider's hitpoints by 4%.
*On 30/1/2025, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (30/1/2025)|maintenance break]], made it so that [[Rune Giant]]'s damage boost would no longer affect the Ram Rider's Rider.
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Ram Rider's hitpoints by 0.05% and her charge damage by 0.2%. It also allowed the Ram Rider to be affected by [[Rage]].
*On 6/10/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2025)=|Balance Update]], increased the distance required for charging to 2.5 tiles (from 2 tiles).

