==Trivia==
*The weapon that the Ram Rider wields is called a [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bolas bola]. Bolas were most famously used by the gauchos, but have been found in excavations of Pre-Columbian settlements, especially in Patagonia, where indigenous peoples used them to catch guanacos and rheas.
*The ram that she rides resembles an "''Ovis canadensis''" ([https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bighorn_sheep bighorn sheep]) and similar species. Bighorn sheep have large compact curved horns and attack by charging towards their target with their horns, similarly to the Ram Rider's ram in Clash Royale. 
*The Ram Rider is 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], [[Baby Dragon]], [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Inferno Dragon]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
**Unlike her [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Ram_Rider Clash of Clans counterpart], the Ram Rider in Clash Royale only attacks with her ram once, with the Ram Rider herself attacking the target afterwards from range. In addition, the ram is able to apply a slow effect to its target.
**The appearance of the Ram Rider is also different in Clash Royale, appearing without holiday decorations, or as a cookie.
*The Ram Rider is one of the first troop [[cards]] to receive a card render, alongside the [[Archers]], [[Knight]], [[Goblins]], Bomber, [[Skeletons]], [[Barbarians]], Bats, [[Royal Recruits]], Skeleton Barrel, [[Rascals]], [[Musketeer]], [[Giant]], [[Valkyrie]], [[Wizard]], [[Flying Machine]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Dart Goblin]], Zappies, [[Elixir Golem]], Baby Dragon, [[Skeleton Army]], [[Witch]], [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], Giant Skeleton, [[Goblin Giant]], [[Hunter]], [[Electro Dragon]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Bowler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Mega Knight]], Miner, Royal Ghost, Ice Wizard, [[Magic Archer]], [[Bandit]], [[Lava Hound]], Night Witch, and [[Fisherman]].
*She is 1 of 5 troops that have a charge, the others being Battle Ram, [[Dark Prince]], Prince, and [[Raging Prince]].
*The Ram Rider is 1 of 8 troops that can jump over the river, the others being Hog Rider, Royal Hogs, Dark Prince, Prince, Raging Prince, [[Mother Witch|Cursed Hog]], and [[Santa Hog Rider]].
*The Ram Rider is 1 of 2 troops with the “Ranged Ground & Air targeting unit riding on Melee Building targeting unit” pattern, the other being the Goblin Giant. However, the Rider cannot attack alone if the Ram is destroyed, and only the Ram can attack [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]].
*In the Dutch and Norwegian language settings of the game, the Ram Rider's name translates to "Buck Rider". In the Indonesian and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Ram Rider's name translates to "Sheep Rider". In the Italian, French, Portuguese, Thai, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Ram Rider's name translates to "Ram Tamer", "Cavalier", "Sheep Tamer", "Sheepwoman", and "City Breaker" respectively. In both the Simplified Chinese and the Traditional Chinese language setting, the Ram Rider's name translates to "[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barbary_sheep Barbary sheep] Knight".
**''Ammotragus lervia'', the common names of which include Barbary sheep, inhabits a range across North Africa.
*The Ram Rider has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Ram Rider is 1 of 22 troops that has been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Skeletons, [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], Bats, [[Elite Barbarians]], Firecracker, Rascal Girls, Royal Hogs, [[Heal Spirit]], Elixir Golem, [[Guards]], Prince, Balloon, [[Golem]], Wall Breakers, [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], Royal Ghost, Bandit, [[Lumberjack]], [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
**The Ram Rider is 1 of 14 troops that has been featured with a [[Buff#Rage|Rage]] [[buff]], the others being [[Electro Spirit]], Giant, Zappies, Guards, Giant Skeleton, Goblin Giant, Electro Dragon, Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], Mega Knight, [[Electro Wizard]], [[Sparky]], and Royal Ghost.
*The Rider on the Ram is the only troop in the game that only attacks troops.
*When deployed, the Ram Rider will say "''Out of my way!''".
**The Ram Rider is 1 of 24 troops that speak distinct words when on the field, the others being [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], [[Mega Minion]], Wizard, Hog Rider, P.E.K.K.A., Dark Prince, Bowler, Electro Wizard, [[Princess]], Ice Wizard, Magic Archer, Lumberjack, Mother Witch, Fisherman, [[Goblin Machine]], [[Super Mini P.E.K.K.A.]], Santa Hog Rider, [[Super Magic Archer]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Boss Bandit]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Terry]].
*The Ram Rider is 1 of 10 cards to have an alliterative name, the others being the Royal Recruits, [[Goblin Gang]], Mega Minion, Goblin Giant, Cannon Cart, [[Barbarian Barrel]], [[Dagger Duchess]], [[Boss Bandit]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
*According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=RamRiderComic.jpg strip], the Ram Rider is the Hog Rider's sister.
*The Ram Rider, Phoenix, Lumberjack, and the Fisherman are the only normal spawning {{Rarity|Legendary}} troops that do not fall from the sky when deployed.
*The Ram Rider is the subject of certain cosmetics in the game. More specifically:
**The Ram Rider is the subject of 3 [[Emotes]]. Her ram is also the subject of 2 Emotes.
**The Ram Rider is the subject of a [[King's Tower|Tower Skin]].
**The Ram Rider is the subject of a few [[Battle Banners|Battle Banner]] items.
***The Riders decoration is created by Myoho.
*The Ram Rider was featured in the winning [[Battle Decks|deck]] of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/vRrgTfqRdpw?si=YDASUydL7qNm9QZz Clash Royale League 2023 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.
*The original concept for the Ram Rider was a Wolf Rider troop that used a bow instead of a bola.<ref>https://x.com/supercell/status/1912137641379717337</ref> However, it was replaced with the Ram Rider for unknown reasons.
**Supposedly, part of the reasoning was that there wasn't an easy explanation for having the wolf deal damage to towers.

